h&#39;ing Period/Huang Li-chou\">Huang Li-chou</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367270\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367270\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3640009</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 1 \u2014 Huang Fang-tu</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">Earl Swisher</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"339\" data-page-number=\"339\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/351\" data-page-index=\"351\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/351\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;351\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>HUANG</b> Fang-tu \u9ec3\u82b3\u5ea6 (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u58fd\u5dd6), d. Nov. 22, 1675 age 25 (<i>sui</i>), eldest son of <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Huang_Wu\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Huang Wu\">Huang Wu</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>], Ch'ing general, was a native of Pring-ho, Fukien. When his father died (1674) Huang Fang-tu outwardly accepted <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/K%C3%AAng_Ching-chung\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/K\u00eang Ching-chung\">K\u00eang Ching-chung's</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] invitation to join in the rebellion but secretly recruited 6,000 volunteers to defend Chang-chou, and at the same time reported his decision to Peking. The Emperor authorized his succession to the dukedom of Hai-ch'\u00eang (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Huang_Wu\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Huang Wu\">Huang Wu</a></span>) and charged him to join the government forces in the defense of Fukien. He attempted to resist K\u00eang Ching-chung and to conciliate <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Ch%C3%AAng_Ching\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ch\u00eang Ching\">Ch\u00eang Ching</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>], but when the two rebels joined forces his dual policy collapsed. He made a brilliant defense of Chang-chou, and sent his cousin <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Huang_Fang-t%27ai\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Huang Fang-t&#39;ai\">Huang Fang-t'ai</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] to meet a relieving force from Kwangtung. Unable to hold out until relief came, he drowned himself in the well of K'ai-y\u00fcan monastery \u958b\u5143\u5bfa, November 22, 1675, at the age of twenty-five (<i>sui</i>). More than thirty of his relatives, including his mother, wife, and two younger brothers also committed suicide, as did several of his officers. The Emperor conferred on him the posthumous rank of prince, the name\n&#32;<span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"340\" data-page-number=\"340\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/352\" data-page-index=\"352\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/352\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;352\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span>Chung-yung \u5fe0\u52c7, and burial with the rites of a <i>Ch\u00fcn-wang</i> or a prince of the second degree.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[4/118/24a; see bibliography for <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Huang_Wu\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Huang Wu\">Huang Wu</a></span>.]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Earl Swisher</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ch\u00eang Ching"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Huang Fang-t'ai"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Huang Li-chou"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Huang Wu"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/K\u00eang Ching-chung"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Earl Swisher"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 1\n | onlysection = huang fang-tu\n | previous = Huang Fang-t'ai\n | next     = Huang Li-chou\n | from     = 351\n | to       = 352\n | notes    =\n | section_author = Earl Swisher\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Huang Fang-tu}}"}}}